<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Longbow</h1>
<p>Average Length: 5.5 to 6 feet.
Type of Weapon: Missile Weapon.
Commonly used by: Archers.
</p><p>These bows were the traditional bows that are often used today, minus the pulleys and contraptions. They had decent range and accounted, with other distance weapons, for about half of all deaths in combat. Arrows made deep puncture wounds that infected easily, another danger. Usually, if an archer was captured and ransomed, his thumb and forefinger would be cut off to ensure that he would never shoot again.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="In_Valhalla">In Valhalla</span></h2>
<p>In Valhalla a longbow uses the bow skill, one of the special weapons (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weapons</a>): it pierces, it leans on dexterity, with some strength, and it is slow to shoot. You shoot arrows with it (see <a cmd='#'>Help Shoot</a>). It is taught by the rangers from guild level 10.
</p><p><br />
